# Credentials. Every fetch script on this site reads its key from the
# environment and never from disk (beauty/netutil.py says so in as many
# words), and the .env that holds them lives in the home directory, outside
# this repo. That is where it happens to be, not a rule the repo enforces:
# a .env copied in here for convenience would be tracked by default. Added
# 2026-09-08, the day beauty/fetch_openalex.py first ran with a key.
.env
